WEBVTT

00:00.292 --> 00:03.580
<i>♪ It seems today that all you see ♪</i>

00:03.581 --> 00:06.882
<i>♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪</i>

00:06.883 --> 00:10.452
<i>♪ But where are those good
old-fashioned values ♪</i>

00:10.453 --> 00:13.455
<i>♪ On which we used to rely? ♪</i>

00:13.456 --> 00:16.959
<i>♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪</i>

00:16.960 --> 00:20.362
<i>♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪</i>

00:20.363 --> 00:21.897
<i>♪ All the things that make us ♪</i>

00:21.898 --> 00:23.366
<i>♪ Laugh and cry ♪</i>

00:23.367 --> 00:28.053
<i>♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪</i>

00:33.951 --> 00:37.286
<i>This program is brought
to you by Fruit Bouquets.</i>

00:37.287 --> 00:40.120
<i>Got a birthday coming up for
someone you absolutely hate?</i>

00:40.121 --> 00:41.956
<i>Why not tell them to go screw themselves</i>

00:41.957 --> 00:43.926
<i>by sending a giant Fruit Bouquet?</i>

00:43.927 --> 00:45.728
<i>With just a few clicks, you'll be able</i>

00:45.729 --> 00:48.798
<i>to send someone 14 pounds of
unwanted decorative produce</i>

00:48.799 --> 00:51.400
<i>that will go bad within
an hour of arrival!</i>

00:51.401 --> 00:53.636
Hungry for a strangely-warm strawberry?

00:53.637 --> 00:57.040
How about a hard green wedge
or a slime-glazed melon ball?

00:57.041 --> 00:58.974
Well, we have all these gross things.

00:58.975 --> 01:00.876
Order now and make someone feel guilty

01:00.877 --> 01:03.245
about throwing it straight into
the trash six hours later.

01:03.246 --> 01:06.548
Fruit Bouquets: the rotting
gift with flies on it!

01:06.549 --> 01:09.118
Okay, I'm heading out for ladies' night.

01:09.119 --> 01:10.920
There's a casserole in the refrigerator.

01:10.921 --> 01:12.454
I'll be home at 11:00.

01:12.455 --> 01:13.889
- Hey, Lois?
- Yeah?

01:13.890 --> 01:16.392
How would you find out the
name of the actual actress

01:16.393 --> 01:18.260
who plays the AT&T chick?

01:18.261 --> 01:20.396
I left a list of hot commercial girls

01:20.397 --> 01:21.798
on the refrigerator.

01:21.799 --> 01:24.067
What is this "refrigerator"
you keep mentioning?

01:24.068 --> 01:25.902
Are you talking about
the sandwich house?

01:25.903 --> 01:28.103
I guess I'm not the only person

01:28.104 --> 01:29.406
with a useless husband.

01:29.407 --> 01:31.549
I mean, look at Mrs. Butterworth.

01:31.550 --> 01:34.152
I still don't understand why
we couldn't take my last name.

01:34.153 --> 01:37.222
Well, my last name helps
keep a roof over our head

01:37.223 --> 01:38.991
and pays for your hobby.

01:38.992 --> 01:40.158
Hobby?

01:41.327 --> 01:42.727
Oh, look at that.

01:42.728 --> 01:44.896
My business line is ringing.

01:44.897 --> 01:47.232
Hello? Lamps That Look
Like Soccer Balls.

01:47.233 --> 01:48.900
Yes?

01:48.901 --> 01:51.636
Okay. How many would you like to return?

01:51.637 --> 01:55.173
Yeah, just send them here, care of...

01:55.174 --> 01:57.294
Mr. Butterworth.

02:02.582 --> 02:04.849
Ah, it's so nice getting
out of the house.

02:04.850 --> 02:08.087
If I had to change one more
diaper, I was gonna lose it.

02:08.088 --> 02:09.955
I'm in exactly the same boat.

02:09.956 --> 02:11.856
I mean, what would our husbands do

02:11.857 --> 02:13.825
if they had to change their own diapers?

02:13.826 --> 02:16.327
Different boat, Bonnie.
Much different boat.

02:16.328 --> 02:18.129
Hey, I got an idea.

02:18.130 --> 02:19.464
Let's crank call them.

02:19.465 --> 02:21.533
Me first.

02:21.534 --> 02:24.035
You're weak, Cleveland!

02:24.036 --> 02:25.937
You're worthless and weak!

02:27.273 --> 02:28.606
You found Brown.

02:28.607 --> 02:29.874
Hello, Cleveland.

02:29.875 --> 02:31.176
This is Michelle Obama.

02:31.177 --> 02:32.378
<i>It is?!</i>

02:32.379 --> 02:34.712
Yes. I received all your letters,

02:34.713 --> 02:36.981
<i>and I do like your mustache.</i>

02:36.982 --> 02:40.051
Oh. I've been doing all
your arm exercises.

02:40.052 --> 02:43.289
<i>Thank you, but those won't
work on your fat arms.</i>

02:43.290 --> 02:45.156
How do you know my arms are fat?

02:45.157 --> 02:47.625
I deliberately left them
out of all the photos.

02:47.626 --> 02:50.728
<i>You're eating a pie on the
toilet, aren't you, Cleveland?</i>

02:50.729 --> 02:53.398
Who is this? Is this a Jerky Boy?!

02:53.399 --> 02:55.066
It's your wife, you big dummy!

02:59.638 --> 03:02.740
I used to have my own show.

03:05.811 --> 03:07.812
Hello?

03:07.813 --> 03:09.515
Hello. Is this Joe Swanson?

03:09.516 --> 03:11.049
Wait. You can talk normal?

03:11.050 --> 03:12.517
What do you mean?

03:12.518 --> 03:13.818
Never mind.

03:13.819 --> 03:15.688
We're calling from WQHG,

03:15.689 --> 03:17.088
Quahog's Hottest Hits.

03:17.089 --> 03:19.924
And we'll give you $500 if
you can sing Britney Spears'

03:19.925 --> 03:22.227
"I'm Not A Girl, Not Yet A Woman."

03:22.228 --> 03:23.828
You've got ten seconds to...

03:23.829 --> 03:27.265
<i>♪ I'm not a girl, not yet a woman ♪</i>

03:27.266 --> 03:30.034
<i>♪ All I need is time... ♪</i>

03:30.035 --> 03:32.203
Oh, but you have to be able to walk.

03:32.204 --> 03:33.605
<i>Aw, nuts.</i>

03:35.341 --> 03:37.041
Okay, my turn! My turn!

03:39.745 --> 03:42.180
Hello. Don't say anything
about the 1998 Oscars.

03:42.181 --> 03:43.615
I'm watching it now.

03:43.616 --> 03:45.950
<i>Hello, is this Peter Griffin?</i>

03:45.951 --> 03:48.453
If this is the fracking
people, I have made it clear

03:48.454 --> 03:50.588
that I am 100% on board.

03:50.589 --> 03:52.857
<i>No, my name is Rebecca.</i>

03:52.858 --> 03:54.592
<i>You've never met me before</i>

03:54.593 --> 03:58.815
<i>and probably don't even know I
exist, but you're my father.</i>

03:59.815 --> 04:01.467
Hello?

04:01.468 --> 04:03.968
<i>How'd you get this number? Don't
you ever call here again!</i>

04:03.969 --> 04:05.738
What the hell?!

04:05.739 --> 04:07.640
He just got mad and hung up.

04:07.641 --> 04:09.307
He what? Why?

04:09.308 --> 04:11.142
I don't know. He sounded weird.

04:11.143 --> 04:13.711
Like when he was an NFL
announcer and had to pretend

04:13.712 --> 04:16.481
he cared about the shows after the game.

04:16.482 --> 04:18.651
Patriots calling their
third and final timeout.

04:18.652 --> 04:20.585
Hey, after the game, keep it here

04:20.586 --> 04:22.553
<i>for an all-new Madam Secretary.</i>

04:22.554 --> 04:24.222
Tonight, Madam Secretary faces

04:24.223 --> 04:26.391
an international crisis in Pakistan,

04:26.392 --> 04:28.894
while her teenage daughter
faces her own crisis

04:28.895 --> 04:30.462
finding a date for the prom.

04:30.463 --> 04:32.264
<i>Madam Secretary, tonight on CBS.</i>

04:33.633 --> 04:36.286
Is this the longest
time-out of all time?

04:40.322 --> 04:42.407
Hey, Peter.

04:42.408 --> 04:45.176
So, um, anything interesting
happen tonight?

04:45.177 --> 04:48.447
Yup. I finally peed that chunk
of poo off the side of the bowl.

04:48.448 --> 04:50.782
You know the one you've
been yelling at me about?

04:50.783 --> 04:52.851
Nobody... called or anything?

04:52.852 --> 04:55.120
Nope. So, hey, uh, are you tipsy enough

04:55.121 --> 04:57.588
to let me have lazy Tony Soprano sex?

04:57.589 --> 04:59.524
You know, where-where I just lie there

04:59.525 --> 05:02.360
and arch my hips a little bit
and breathe like a dying whale?

05:02.361 --> 05:03.695
Uh, I don't know.

05:03.696 --> 05:05.798
All right, well, just in
case, I'll be upstairs

05:05.799 --> 05:09.033
getting into my boxers and black socks.

05:24.332 --> 05:25.651
Do you think it's possible

05:25.652 --> 05:28.187
he actually has an illegitimate child?

05:28.188 --> 05:30.055
I don't know, but something's going on,

05:30.056 --> 05:32.657
because I'm telling you,
he lied right to my face.

05:32.658 --> 05:35.727
Sometimes friends put
wine out for each other.

05:35.728 --> 05:37.062
I just don't understand it.

05:37.063 --> 05:39.298
I mean, we don't keep
secrets in this house.

05:39.299 --> 05:42.085
We didn't even keep the
Pop Secret's secret.

05:44.019 --> 05:46.070
Psst. Hey, did you hear?

05:46.071 --> 05:47.238
Hear what?

05:47.239 --> 05:49.240
Orville Redenbacher is gay.

05:49.241 --> 05:50.808
But he has a son.

05:50.809 --> 05:52.144
He's in the commercial.

05:52.145 --> 05:54.680
His son's gay, too. They're both gay.

05:54.681 --> 05:57.548
They have sex parties
in the Hollywood Hills.

05:57.549 --> 05:59.884
It sounds like you're
just making up stories

05:59.885 --> 06:01.419
about your competitors.

06:01.420 --> 06:02.920
You're gay, too.

06:02.921 --> 06:04.555
What?

06:04.556 --> 06:07.492
Aah! You're a psycho!

06:07.493 --> 06:09.394
Dad, you're never gonna believe what...

06:09.395 --> 06:12.614
Chris, meet Orville Redenbacher
and his son. Watch.

06:15.950 --> 06:18.603
And that's where we get the expression

06:18.604 --> 06:21.240
"gay as a bag of popcorn."

06:21.241 --> 06:22.841
All right, I'll see you later.

06:22.842 --> 06:24.243
What? Where are you going?

06:24.244 --> 06:27.044
Laser tag orientation.

06:27.045 --> 06:28.846
Well, that's obviously not true.

06:28.847 --> 06:30.782
Yeah, that boy got lie-arrhea.

06:30.783 --> 06:32.617
Oh, my God. I-I got to follow him,

06:32.618 --> 06:34.252
find out where he's really going.

06:34.253 --> 06:35.788
Good idea. If I was you,

06:35.789 --> 06:37.423
I'd stick to him like glue-arrhea.

06:37.424 --> 06:40.793
Okay, I think I'm starting
to crack your code.

06:40.794 --> 06:42.628
Quick, Brian, I need your car.

06:42.629 --> 06:43.961
I don't know, Lois.

06:43.962 --> 06:46.031
You're not on the insurance,
and I don't think that...

06:54.140 --> 06:55.974
Fruit Bouquet for Brian Griffin?

06:55.975 --> 06:58.242
Happy birthday, buddy.

07:17.847 --> 07:19.916
What the hell?

07:21.183 --> 07:23.401
Peter, what are you doing here?

07:23.402 --> 07:24.769
Lois! Uh, uh...

07:24.770 --> 07:26.805
I was... I'm just, uh, shopping.

07:26.806 --> 07:29.106
Yeah, I'll-I'll take a
large sperm, please.

07:29.107 --> 07:31.008
Nice going, now you've ruined Christmas.

07:31.009 --> 07:34.278
Peter Griffin, you tell me
what's going on right now.

07:34.279 --> 07:37.582
Okay, fine, I'll be honest with you.

07:37.583 --> 07:41.019
A long while back, just
before we got married,

07:41.020 --> 07:42.753
I was a little short of cash.

07:42.754 --> 07:44.423
What, to buy our rings?

07:44.424 --> 07:47.693
No, I wanted to pay for dial-up
modem impression classes. See?

07:59.287 --> 08:01.673
Wow, that's pretty good. I...

08:01.674 --> 08:03.508
You've got mail.

08:03.509 --> 08:06.210
Okay, but hang on. You
were a sperm donor?

08:06.211 --> 08:07.879
Yeah, I'd-I'd almost forgotten about it,

08:07.880 --> 08:10.681
but then last night, I get
this call from a woman

08:10.682 --> 08:12.049
who says she's my daughter.

08:12.050 --> 08:14.553
Peter, that was me. I
was prank calling you.

08:14.554 --> 08:15.721
You what?!

08:15.722 --> 08:17.622
I can't believe you would do that to me!

08:17.623 --> 08:19.123
Can you guys argue elsewhere?

08:19.124 --> 08:21.058
You're making it tough
to finish in here.

08:21.059 --> 08:23.461
No, fight louder! Call her a bitch!

08:23.462 --> 08:24.862
But I don't understand.

08:24.863 --> 08:26.397
Why did you come here today?

08:26.398 --> 08:28.299
'Cause that call last
night gave me a scare.

08:28.300 --> 08:30.468
I figured if I do have a kid out there,

08:30.469 --> 08:32.904
I want to make sure they're not
giving out my information.

08:32.905 --> 08:34.806
They're not supposed
to; I signed a form.

08:34.807 --> 08:36.008
Hold on, Peter.

08:36.009 --> 08:37.409
I'm sorry I tricked you,

08:37.410 --> 08:39.912
but if you do have a child out there,

08:39.913 --> 08:42.414
isn't it only fair to let
him or her meet you?

08:42.415 --> 08:45.250
Eh, maybe you're right.

08:45.251 --> 08:46.717
I mean, as long as we're here,

08:46.718 --> 08:48.920
maybe you should sign a consent form.

08:48.921 --> 08:50.254
Okay, yeah.

08:50.255 --> 08:52.223
All right, I'll do it.

08:52.224 --> 08:53.424
You know what?

08:53.425 --> 08:55.726
It feels good doing
something nice for others.

08:55.727 --> 08:58.096
Like when I was a mentor for Kid Rock.

08:58.097 --> 09:00.566
Okay, I took a leak into
this can of Busch Light

09:00.567 --> 09:01.866
without spilling.

09:01.867 --> 09:03.101
You're ready.

09:03.102 --> 09:04.937
You don't need me anymore.

09:04.938 --> 09:06.404
Will I see you again, Peter?

09:06.405 --> 09:08.941
Wherever a father weighs
less than his daughter,

09:08.942 --> 09:10.241
I'll be there.

09:10.242 --> 09:12.677
Wherever someone has a
banner for a football team

09:12.678 --> 09:15.246
as a curtain, I'll be there.

09:15.247 --> 09:17.682
Wherever there's a fight
in a Waffle House,

09:17.683 --> 09:19.451
I'll be there.

09:19.452 --> 09:20.434
Now go.

09:20.435 --> 09:23.472
People need a concert to go
to after the water park.

09:34.782 --> 09:37.535
Hi, is, uh, is Peter Griffin here?

09:37.536 --> 09:39.303
Oh, my God.

09:39.304 --> 09:40.771
Is everything okay?

09:40.772 --> 09:43.240
Yes, it's just... you look just like...

09:43.241 --> 09:45.576
What's going on? Who's this supermodel?

09:45.577 --> 09:47.379
I'm Katie.

09:47.380 --> 09:48.879
I'm your daughter.

09:48.880 --> 09:50.314
You're what?

09:50.315 --> 09:51.415
Holy crap!

09:51.416 --> 09:53.150
Yeah, I hope you don't mind the drop-in,

09:53.151 --> 09:56.153
but the, uh, the sperm bank said
it was okay to contact you.

09:56.154 --> 09:59.323
Wow, I guess, I guess I just
didn't expect this so soon.

09:59.324 --> 10:01.392
Well, we were all pretty
excited to meet you.

10:01.393 --> 10:03.112
What do you mean "we"?

10:09.450 --> 10:11.302
Hi, Dad!

10:11.303 --> 10:14.139
We're all your children.
We came from your semen.

10:14.140 --> 10:16.073
"Semen."

10:17.809 --> 10:19.459
- "Semen."
- "Semen."

10:19.460 --> 10:21.178
Ha-ha!

10:21.179 --> 10:23.447
Oh, sorry. Wrong house.

10:23.448 --> 10:25.449
Look, Eddie's at the wrong house.

10:25.450 --> 10:27.267
- Ha-ha!
- Ha-ha!

10:27.268 --> 10:28.705
- Ha-ha!
- Ha-ha!

10:37.210 --> 10:40.064
Peter, how many times
were you a sperm donor?

10:40.065 --> 10:43.602
<i>Only once, but I had just seen
Uma Thurman in Beautiful Girls,</i>

10:43.603 --> 10:45.171
so it was kind of a ka-blamo.

10:45.172 --> 10:48.273
You ever seen those videos where
they put Mentos in Diet Coke?

10:48.274 --> 10:50.275
Uh, listen, I want all of you to know

10:50.276 --> 10:52.044
how happy we are to meet you.

10:52.045 --> 10:55.529
In fact, this calls for a celebration.

10:55.530 --> 10:57.365
Can you all stay for dinner?

10:57.366 --> 10:59.634
Aw, we'd love that. Wouldn't we, guys?

10:59.635 --> 11:00.735
Yeah, absolutely.

11:00.736 --> 11:01.736
You said it, babe.

11:01.737 --> 11:03.804
Yeah, Chinese Peter very hungry.

11:03.805 --> 11:05.439
Whoa, whoa, whoa, slow down there, Lois.

11:05.440 --> 11:07.742
Just 'cause they're my kids
and they all look like me

11:07.743 --> 11:09.644
doesn't mean we have anything in common.

11:16.151 --> 11:17.653
Daddy.

11:31.684 --> 11:36.089
I've never felt proud of any
of my children until now.

11:40.158 --> 11:41.676
This is so exciting.

11:41.677 --> 11:45.079
For years, I have dreamed of
one day traveling from Bavaria

11:45.080 --> 11:47.448
to play the accordion
for my birth family.

11:47.449 --> 11:48.449
May I?

11:53.251 --> 11:55.114
I have just one question for you.

11:55.857 --> 11:58.159
What are those?!

11:58.160 --> 12:00.161
Oh, I get that because this comedy

12:00.162 --> 12:02.029
has just made it to Germany.

12:02.030 --> 12:04.665
Wow, you look exactly like me.

12:04.666 --> 12:06.534
Yes, I'm not actually part

12:06.535 --> 12:08.202
of sperm donation thing.

12:08.203 --> 12:09.837
I'm your secret clone.

12:09.838 --> 12:13.359
<i>We have been Orphan Black-ed
and you soon will be dead.</i>

12:18.530 --> 12:20.015
Meg, where are you?

12:20.016 --> 12:21.700
I'm right here, Mom.

12:22.734 --> 12:24.852
Well, look at your fine ass.

12:24.853 --> 12:26.355
Are you talking to me?

12:26.356 --> 12:27.621
Damn right.

12:27.622 --> 12:29.057
I've been looking
around this whole house

12:29.058 --> 12:30.158
for something to nibble on.

12:30.159 --> 12:31.459
I think I just found it.

12:31.460 --> 12:34.362
So many confusing feelings!

12:34.363 --> 12:35.731
- Dad.
- Sex.

12:35.732 --> 12:36.865
Black woman.

12:36.866 --> 12:39.134
Historically-low mortgage rates.

12:39.135 --> 12:42.069
Ah! I got to go buy a house.

12:42.070 --> 12:43.237
Lois, Lois.

12:43.238 --> 12:45.072
Can I keep the little person Peter?

12:45.073 --> 12:46.808
No. They're too much work.

12:46.809 --> 12:48.543
But I'll take care of it. I promise.

12:48.544 --> 12:50.911
You always say that, and
I'm the one who ends up

12:50.912 --> 12:53.247
feeding him and walking him
and doing all the clean up.

12:53.248 --> 12:55.183
Excuse me, I'm a candidate

12:55.184 --> 12:57.552
for a doctorate in Classics at Wesleyan.

12:57.553 --> 12:59.739
It talks! Lois, it talks!

13:04.843 --> 13:06.394
Whoa, that was close.

13:06.395 --> 13:08.896
You almost dipped one of
your yabbos in the marinara.

13:08.897 --> 13:10.164
Let me help you with those.

13:10.165 --> 13:12.433
Well, thank you. That's so sweet.

13:12.434 --> 13:14.903
You're the first person who
looks anything like my husband

13:14.904 --> 13:16.605
who's offered to help in any way.

13:16.606 --> 13:18.173
Oh, you must be Peter's wife, Lois.

13:18.174 --> 13:19.173
I'm Larry.

13:19.174 --> 13:21.776
It's nice to meet you, Larry.

13:21.777 --> 13:24.463
Weird hands-full pinky shake?

13:25.931 --> 13:28.350
I got to tell you, it's so strange,

13:28.351 --> 13:31.285
you look so much like Peter
when I first met him.

13:31.286 --> 13:33.587
Well, I'm guessing you look
exactly the same, too.

13:33.588 --> 13:34.923
You're in such great shape.

13:34.924 --> 13:38.427
Well, I do have tiny blue
weights in my garage.

13:47.552 --> 13:49.036
Oh, hi, Larry.

13:49.037 --> 13:50.638
Hi, Lois. Is Peter here?

13:50.639 --> 13:52.707
Larry, it's only 2:00 in the afternoon.

13:52.708 --> 13:54.809
Peter's still sleeping
off last night's party.

13:54.810 --> 13:57.913
Then why... why are you still
in your pajamas and bathrobe?

13:57.914 --> 14:00.148
Oh, that's because I'm depressed.

14:00.149 --> 14:02.650
Is that why that sad
Shel Silverstein blob

14:02.651 --> 14:03.818
is following you around?

14:03.819 --> 14:06.654
Who would ever me?

14:06.655 --> 14:08.088
Anyway, we didn't really get a chance

14:08.089 --> 14:09.924
to finish our conversation yesterday,

14:09.925 --> 14:12.092
and I thought maybe we could
grab some lunch together.

14:12.093 --> 14:15.896
Huh. That would give me a
reason to get dressed today.

14:15.897 --> 14:18.666
Oh. Would you, uh, like to join us?

14:18.667 --> 14:21.836
That didn't sound like
a real invitation.

14:21.837 --> 14:25.358
See, this is why no one
ever wants to you.

14:29.427 --> 14:31.413
Thank you again for lunch, Larry.

14:31.414 --> 14:34.014
Sorry I drew so many Nazi
symbols on the place mat.

14:34.015 --> 14:35.951
- I was just nervous.
- That's okay.

14:35.952 --> 14:38.752
I just wish we hadn't gone
to a kosher restaurant.

14:38.753 --> 14:40.087
Ugh, but look at me.

14:40.088 --> 14:41.789
I got ice cream all over my fingers.

14:41.790 --> 14:43.124
Do you have a napkin?

14:43.125 --> 14:45.545
No, but let me help you clean it off.

14:54.686 --> 14:57.606
Larry, are you turned on or starving?

14:57.607 --> 14:59.025
Can't it be both?

15:10.051 --> 15:11.452
- Mm.
- Mm.

15:11.453 --> 15:14.021
Wow, Larry, that was unexpected.

15:14.022 --> 15:15.723
Shh, we'll discuss this later.

15:15.724 --> 15:17.958
- I have to get back to my high school...
- Oh.

15:17.959 --> 15:19.493
- Where I work...
- Oh.

15:19.494 --> 15:20.794
- As a janitor...
- Oh.

15:20.795 --> 15:23.063
- To pay for medical school...
- Oh.

15:23.064 --> 15:25.066
- That I'm building...
- Oh!

15:25.067 --> 15:27.086
- Out of Popsicle sticks.
- Oh.

15:34.584 --> 15:37.569
That big one doesn't
blink a lot, does he?

15:37.570 --> 15:38.736
Hey, Lois, where's your purse?

15:38.737 --> 15:40.564
Me and some of my kids
are going to the movies.

15:40.565 --> 15:42.507
By the way, Dwarf Peter died.

15:42.508 --> 15:44.568
I didn't know what he ate,
so I gave him nothing.

15:44.569 --> 15:46.611
His name was Tyler.

15:46.612 --> 15:47.779
He had a name.

15:47.780 --> 15:50.115
Everything you say, you say with pride.

15:50.116 --> 15:51.283
I like that about you.

15:51.284 --> 15:52.534
Anyway, where's Larry?

15:52.535 --> 15:53.827
Maybe he wants to go to the movie.

15:53.828 --> 15:54.828
Larry?

15:54.829 --> 15:56.872
Why would I know where Larry is?

15:56.873 --> 15:57.914
And who is Larry?

15:57.915 --> 15:58.957
Well, never mind.

15:58.958 --> 16:00.542
All right, everybody bring your phones

16:00.543 --> 16:02.570
so we can text each
other during the movie.

16:06.715 --> 16:09.201
Wow, you want to tell me what that was?

16:09.202 --> 16:12.937
Oh, Brian, Larry and I sort
of crossed a line yesterday.

16:12.938 --> 16:15.274
I don't know, he's just
so sweet and fun-loving,

16:15.275 --> 16:16.349
and for God's sake,

16:16.350 --> 16:18.584
he looks just like Peter
did when he was his age.

16:18.585 --> 16:19.752
Yeah, but...?

16:19.753 --> 16:23.289
Well, he kissed me and
I kind of let him.

16:23.290 --> 16:26.193
I told him it could never
happen again and that...

16:26.194 --> 16:27.693
What are you doing?

16:27.694 --> 16:30.930
Oh, I-I thought that was kind of
like, "I'm open for business."

16:30.931 --> 16:33.766
No! I'm confiding in a friend.

16:33.767 --> 16:36.636
Oh! You're the safe friend.

16:36.637 --> 16:39.872
Look, I feel awful about it,
but I told Larry that was it,

16:39.873 --> 16:42.108
and we couldn't be anything
more than friends.

16:42.109 --> 16:43.309
So, you're still gonna see him?

16:43.310 --> 16:45.745
Yes, of course; he's a nice young man

16:45.746 --> 16:47.446
and he's practically family.

16:47.447 --> 16:48.948
Lois!

16:48.949 --> 16:51.217
No! Zoloft Blob, don't!

16:58.925 --> 17:00.259
Is everything okay?

17:00.260 --> 17:02.928
Yeah, I-I'm fine, I just
hurt my neck this morning

17:02.929 --> 17:05.631
<i>vigorously nodding
approval to Judge Judy.</i>

17:05.632 --> 17:07.933
Okay, all right, the doctor is in.

17:07.934 --> 17:09.669
Come on, back it up over here.

17:09.670 --> 17:11.404
Somebody's got a neck massage coming.

17:11.405 --> 17:12.638
Ah, right there.

17:12.639 --> 17:14.908
Okay, but let's keep this friendly.

17:14.909 --> 17:16.910
You can choke me for just a second.

17:16.911 --> 17:19.445
You know, maybe I should just go
ahead and do your whole back.

17:19.446 --> 17:21.782
Yeah, your bra strap is
getting in the way here.

17:21.783 --> 17:23.801
I'll just bite it off with my teeth.

17:25.836 --> 17:27.987
Lois, is a president
stronger than a king?

17:27.988 --> 17:28.988
What the hell?!

17:28.989 --> 17:30.156
Oh, Peter.

17:30.157 --> 17:32.659
L-Look, calm down. We're just friends.

17:32.660 --> 17:34.760
H-He's just giving me
a friendly massage.

17:34.761 --> 17:36.529
A friendly massage?!

17:36.530 --> 17:38.197
Yeah, and what do you care?

17:38.198 --> 17:40.534
When's the last time you
did anything nice for me?

17:40.535 --> 17:42.968
I ate that gross pasta you made.

17:42.969 --> 17:44.870
I might as well just tell you, Peter.

17:44.871 --> 17:46.640
I'm in love with Lois.

17:46.641 --> 17:48.541
I knew it the moment we kissed.

17:48.542 --> 17:49.543
Kissed?!

17:49.544 --> 17:50.677
Is that true?!

17:50.678 --> 17:51.678
Yes, Peter, but I...

17:51.679 --> 17:53.679
You son of a bitch!

18:17.404 --> 18:19.839
Everybody says, "We don't need
a homeowners' association.

18:19.840 --> 18:21.173
That's stupid, Quagmire."

18:21.174 --> 18:23.860
Well, this is why a
homeowners' association.

18:50.103 --> 18:51.270
What the hell?!

18:51.271 --> 18:52.371
Lois?!

18:52.372 --> 18:53.739
What'd you do that for?

18:53.740 --> 18:56.008
I thought you and him were
girlfriend and boyfriend.

18:56.009 --> 18:58.043
He was not my boyfriend, Peter.

18:58.044 --> 19:00.913
And I wasn't about to stand by
and watch him kick your ass.

19:00.914 --> 19:02.415
I was holding my own there.

19:02.416 --> 19:03.583
You were getting beat up.

19:03.584 --> 19:05.718
No, no, I meant I was
holding my own nuts

19:05.719 --> 19:06.895
so he wouldn't kick them.

19:06.896 --> 19:09.165
But if he's not your
boyfriend, why'd you kiss him?

19:09.166 --> 19:10.733
He kissed me.

19:10.734 --> 19:12.301
And I should've told you.

19:12.302 --> 19:14.970
I'm sorry if I hurt you, Peter.

19:14.971 --> 19:18.174
I guess Larry just reminded me
of a younger version of you,

19:18.175 --> 19:19.675
and the truth is,

19:19.676 --> 19:22.577
I liked that he was paying
me a little attention,

19:22.578 --> 19:24.647
the way you used to.

19:25.748 --> 19:27.782
Maybe I have been
taking you for granted,

19:27.783 --> 19:29.584
but I promise I'll make it up to you.

19:29.585 --> 19:31.419
I'll be the best husband ever.

19:31.420 --> 19:32.988
You already are.

19:32.989 --> 19:34.990
For God's sakes, when
push came to shove,

19:34.991 --> 19:38.360
you stood toe-to-toe with a much
younger man and fought for me.

19:38.361 --> 19:40.495
Oh, hey, by the way, uh,
thanks, all my kids,

19:40.496 --> 19:41.863
for stepping in to help.

19:41.864 --> 19:43.165
Really, really appreciate that.

19:43.166 --> 19:45.433
But you're right, Lois.
I'm gonna change.

19:45.434 --> 19:48.170
I'm gonna do all the stuff for
you that Larry was doing.

19:48.171 --> 19:50.505
No, Peter, I don't need any of that.

19:50.506 --> 19:53.108
At our age, all I'm really
looking for in a husband

19:53.109 --> 19:55.878
is someone who wants to watch
TV with me on a Saturday night

19:55.879 --> 19:58.046
and isn't afraid to
pop a zit on my back.

19:58.047 --> 20:00.048
"Afraid"? I love doing that.

20:00.049 --> 20:01.216
It's like bubble wrap

20:01.217 --> 20:03.385
you get to have sex with
every now and then.

20:03.386 --> 20:06.455
I got a pretty good one
going right now, Peter.

20:06.456 --> 20:08.056
You always do, Lois.

20:08.057 --> 20:09.692
I love you.

20:09.693 --> 20:11.712
Mm.

20:13.812 --> 20:17.232
<i> From that day forward, Peter
and Lois never again...</i>

20:17.233 --> 20:20.220
<i>Ooh, nope, sorry, there's
still another scene left.</i>

20:24.223 --> 20:27.175
Well, Peter, turns out your
initial instinct was right.

20:27.176 --> 20:29.711
You never should've let any
of your children contact you.

20:29.712 --> 20:30.745
You said it.

20:30.746 --> 20:33.215
From now on, I'm making sure my sperm

20:33.216 --> 20:36.685
stays right where it belongs:
in the bathroom sink.

20:39.530 --> 20:44.153
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru

20:55.921 --> 20:57.357
We have fun down here.